{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 1cf42f3b and a7c8072a for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\n1cf42f3b, a used genesis of a private sequence. Choose (b).\n`anchoredCopy` accepts a genesis copy when `fact.seq` is 0 and\n`fact.hash` equals `fact.at.genesis`, and it still requires the\nanchor. Add one check: the copy must pass\n`admitSequenceGenesis(bytes, fact.at)`, and the kind of the\nchecked sequence must equal the recorded kind. The report lists\nthe genesis with the other anchored facts. 5a642337 and 066e49b3\ndo not change. I file option (a) as request RV-1 for its own\nreview after the cutover.\n\na7c8072a, canonical mode at install. Keep it. This is ruled, and\nthe composed component is right. Ruling 788bc90a of 10 November\nsays that every call site which admits a definition into a\nnew-format room passes `canonical: true`, and it names\napplication install. Ruling 8e45aac8 item 4 puts canonical mode\nin head (c+d). Ruling 788bc90a also says that the recorded demo\nrelease in the old spelling is not installable after the cutover.\nSo none of (i), (ii) and (iii) as written. The rule for this head:\n1. No package in the old spelling installs into a new-format\n   room, released or not. Do not build option (iii). The order\n   forbids compatibility code.\n2. A test that installs Grow builds its package from current\n   source, which is canonical since head F, and it uses the pins\n   that F put on main under 0a0286c4. If a Grow digest appears\n   that is not one of those pins, stop and tell me.\n3. If `examples/grow` holds authored source in the old spelling,\n   spell it canonically in this head with Define's `normalize`.\n   If it holds the recorded release, leave its bytes alone.\n4. Keep one test that installs the recorded old-spelling package\n   into a new-format room and expects\n   `invalid-application-package`.\n5. For each fixture or test that read the recorded release or\n   the retained pin as an installable input, the note names it,\n   its acceptance case, and what replaces it.\n6. I sign the new release from canonical source before I\n   recreate the rooms. No test in this head depends on my\n   signature.\n\nThe `seed.creator` audit is accepted. `resolveGenesisSelf` is the\nright repair for a creator that names itself with a null genesis.\nList each comparison that the audit changed in the note.\n\n114ab834 is read. The archive floor stops for good at an entry\nover the ceiling. That fact stays with ARC-1, and ARC-1 keeps its\nplace after the cutover.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}